The Turing ConvRot quantizers, segmented RMSNorm+AdaLN kernel, and W4A8 SM75
GEMM tile/epilogue policy under `csrc/turing/` are derived from comfy-kitchen's
Apache-2.0 CUDA implementation:

  https://github.com/Comfy-Org/comfy-kitchen

The packed Turing W4A8 Tensor Core path uses NVIDIA CUTLASS headers:

  https://github.com/NVIDIA/cutlass

CUTLASS is licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License. Its license text is kept
in `LICENSES/cutlass-LICENSE.txt`.

The SM75 attention sources are derived from wjie98's Apache-2.0 SageAttention
branch `feature/turing-sm75-backend`, commit
`abc695cb9ed9572deb83fd9bb85f0fb815347ebd`, itself derived from SageAttention:

  https://github.com/wjie98/SageAttention/tree/feature/turing-sm75-backend
  https://github.com/thu-ml/SageAttention

The vendored CUDA and Python support is kept under `csrc/turing/sage` and
`svdint4/turing_sage`. Unstable Sage1/Sage2 research is excluded from the
default bindings and documented under `experiments/turing_sage_variants`.
SageAttention is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; its license
text is in `LICENSES/sageattention-LICENSE.txt`.
